What these files are
--------------------

Real Scrivener projects, written by Scrivener 3.5.2 (17486) for Mac on macOS 26.5 on
2026-10-05. The project owner made them for this purpose, following a written protocol,
and typed only their own words into them: no text from a manuscript, a Scrivener
template, Scrivener's tutorial or its manual. They exist so the importer's tests can read
what Scrivener itself writes, where every other fixture in this crate is built by
`scrivener_fixtures` from this project's own reading of the format.

* gt-writing.scriv: prose, comments, footnotes, inline notes, styles, a picture, a
  snapshot and the Trash.
* gt-metadata.scriv: labels, a status list, custom metadata, keywords, targets, a
  collection, bookmarks, a research file and a templates folder.
* gt-footnote-marker.scriv: a project with the footnote marker option turned on.
* gt-writing-v2.scriv: gt-writing as File > Export > as Scrivener 2 Project writes it.
* gt-template.scrivtemplate: gt-metadata as File > Save As Template writes it.
* gt-writing-bak.zip and gt-writing-bak1.zip: two of Scrivener's own automatic backups,
  names unchanged.
* "gt-writing 2026-10-05 15-40.zip": File > Back Up > Back Up To, name unchanged.


What was changed, and nothing else
----------------------------------

`scripts/scrivener_corpus/scrub_ground_truth.py` wrote this directory from the owner's
handover, and refuses to write it unless every check it runs passes. It changed only:

* the Mac's name, in every manifest's `Device` attribute and every lock's `host`, which
  is now `Writers-Mac` everywhere;
* the folder in each lock's `project_path`, which is now
  `/Users/writer/Desktop/skribisto-ground-truth/`;
* the research PDF, a downloaded file that was not the owner's: it is replaced by a
  generated one-page PDF with no metadata, its item is titled `Sample`, and its
  search-index entry holds the new page's text;
* the picture in Scene B, replaced by a generated 225 x 225 palette PNG with no text
  chunks, with the `docs.checksum` lines that were right before recomputed (the one that
  was already stale is kept stale on purpose);
* the rendered preview Scrivener keeps for the Finder, left out, and the hidden files the
  Finder added around the handover, never copied;
* the zips, rebuilt member for member with the same names, order, compression and
  timestamps, and with uid 501 and gid 20.

Git keeps no empty folder, so the empty folders Scrivener makes (one per document, and
an empty `Settings/User/`) are absent from the project folders here; the zips keep
theirs. The importer reads a missing folder exactly as an empty one, and the scrub
script checks that both copies raise the same notices.

The scrub also checks that no byte here, inside the zips and the template's payload
included, holds the Mac's name, the macOS user name, the owner's name, or the downloaded
PDF's title and author. `tests/all/ground_truth.rs` keeps checking, on every test run,
that the device, the lock's host and the home folder are still the scrubbed ones and
that none of the files the Finder adds has come back.
